<title>USA: Procept restructures, cuts staff by 1/3.</title>
<headline>Procept restructures, cuts staff by 1/3.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Procept Inc said Monday it restructured its research and development operations and planned to cut its &quot;cash burn&quot; rate by reducing its staff by a third to 40 employees.  </p>
<p>The Cambridge, Mass.-based company said it would focus on pre-clinical and clinical drug candidates for the prevention of HIV infection, a drug-development program for infectious diseases funded by VacTex.</p>
<p>Procept also said it was seeking corporate partners for two immunosuppression programs.</p>
<p>Procept's shares were up 1/16 at 1-9/16 in afternoon trading.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
